      "zh": {
        "title": "波音 777X 翼尖未展開並鎖定，為何不能起飛？",
        "summary": "波音 777X 可在地面折起翼尖，以配合機場設施。美國聯邦航空總署要求，翼尖未到達飛行位置或尚未鎖定時，飛機除了要警示機組，還必須能阻止起飛。",
        "body": [
          "可折疊的是機翼最外側的翼尖。美國聯邦航空總署（FAA）在 2018 年針對波音 777-8 和 777-9 訂定特別條件，說明翼尖在地面收起可縮短翼展，使飛機仍能使用符合 ICAO E 類標準的登機門。波音的機場規劃文件則顯示，777-9 可在離場滑行時維持翼尖折起，由機組在起飛前展開。",
          "FAA 要求起飛警示系統能提醒機組翼尖未鎖定或位置不正確，並在滑行時顯示翼尖折起的狀態。若翼尖尚未到達飛行位置或未固定，飛機還必須有阻止起飛的手段。這兩道要求分別處理機組警示和起飛防護。"
        ]
      },
      "en": {
        "title": "Why the Boeing 777X cannot take off with its wingtips folded",
        "summary": "The Boeing 777X folds its wingtips on the ground to fit airport infrastructure. FAA requirements call for both a crew warning and a means of preventing takeoff if the wingtips are out of position or unlocked.",
        "body": [
          "Only the outer tips fold. In its 2018 special conditions for the Boeing 777-8 and 777-9, the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration explained that folding the tips on the ground shortens the span for compatibility with ICAO Code E gates. Boeing’s airport planning guide shows that the 777-9 can taxi for departure with the tips folded, with the crew extending them before takeoff.",
          "The FAA requires a takeoff warning for an unlocked or mispositioned wingtip, along with a folded-wingtip indication during taxi. The aircraft must also have a means of preventing takeoff unless its wingtips are positioned and secured for flight. The crew warning and takeoff protection are separate requirements."
        ]
      },
